  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In a cell, the following reactions take place</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mrow><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>77</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>54</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p>The standard electrode potential for the spontaneous reaction in the cell is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>at</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is - (Nearest Integer)</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "23",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The electrode which has more reduction potential will get reduced in spontaneous reaction in the cell. So, spontaneous reaction will be&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>Iron will act as cathode and Iodine will act as anode.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mi>cell</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mfenced><msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mi>RP</mi></msub></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mfenced><msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mi>RP</mi></msub></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>77</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>54</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>23</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>23</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p>"
  }
}